OL,5, At startup the program checks from     
OL,6, which device number it was loaded, and 
OL,7, uses that to store user preferences.   
OL,8, Device numbers 8-11 are supported.     
OL,10,CStand alone PRG editions               
OL,11, Currently onlyFWiC64GandFMeatloaf.     
OL,13, These editions require no installation 
OL,14, and can be run directly by loading and 
OL,15, running the PRG file.                  
OL,17, They use theFpetsciiproxy.nlGserver for
OL,18, both fetching teletext pages and to    
OL,19, store user preferences, which can be   
OL,20, set at program start via theBF2Gkey.   
